From f02567c9568e9b2a857d729ee2588ad6939a5e5f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 06:55:47 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Declare a 3D video's layer as stereo content

While mpv outputs 3D video, that is video-out-params/stereo-in is sbsl
(mpv unpacks every packing to full side by side, left eye first), the
video layer is declared to the compositor through libstereo-declare as
full side by side stereo content of the video class, and removed again
for a 2D video. The layer then has both views, each at the size of the
rectangle of the layer, which is one view's rectangle fitted into the
item, as mpv's render API cannot letterbox each view of a doubled frame.
The layer is only made when libstereo-declare finds the compositor
accepting it.

MpvAbstractItem::stereoVideo and videoRect tell the window about the
3D video and where it is, so that it can fill the rest of the item.

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet via Claude Code
